From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:45:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 29/29] kubelet/stats: report process count and limit on
 FreeBSD

pidlimit.Stats returned nothing outside Linux, so the node summary had no
rlimit stats and the pid.available eviction signal and PIDPressure
condition never fired on FreeBSD. FreeBSD limits processes, not threads:
report min(kern.maxproc, kern.pid_max) as the limit and the number of
processes in kern.proc.proc as the count.
---
 .../stats/pidlimit/pidlimit_freebsd.go        | 73 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../stats/pidlimit/pidlimit_freebsd_test.go   | 55 ++++++++++++++
 .../stats/pidlimit/pidlimit_unsupported.go    |  2 +-
 3 files changed, 129 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 pkg/kubelet/stats/pidlimit/pidlimit_freebsd.go
 create mode 100644 pkg/kubelet/stats/pidlimit/pidlimit_freebsd_test.go

